    "result_text": "The project has a single test class (`AcceptanceTest`, plus its base and a helper), and the full suite is green. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a derived `locality` field to the Owner resource, following the existing pattern used for other derived fields (`membershipTier`, `householdId`, etc.).\n\n**Three changes:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `CITY_REGION` table and a static `locality(String city)` method that returns the canonical region (`Sydney`\u2192`NSW`, `Melbourne`\u2192`VIC`, `Brisbane`\u2192`QLD`), or `\"UNKNOWN\"` for any other city (including `null`), mirroring the other deterministic derivation helpers in this class.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added the `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", ...)` on `toOwnerDto` plus a `formatLocality(owner)` helper that delegates to `Owner.locality(owner.getCity())`.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`. Both acceptance checks pass \u2014 `coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` (Sydney\u2192NSW) and `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` (unlisted city\u2192UNKNOWN).",
