        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change mirrors the established conventions in this codebase exactly:\n\n- **Logic placement is correct.** The city-to-region table and the derivation rule live as a static `locality(String)` method on the `Owner` domain model, alongside the other domain-logic methods (`membershipTier`, etc.). The mapper stays thin, which is right.\n- **It follows the existing pattern precisely.** `OwnerMapper.formatLocality` delegates to `Owner.locality` with a null-guard, exactly as the sibling `formatMembershipTier` \u2192 `Owner.membershipTier`, `formatMembershipNumber`, and `formatHouseholdId` methods do. The `@Mapping(... expression = \"java(formatLocality(owner))\")` line is added in the same block as its peers. A maintainer would find this immediately natural.\n- **No duplication.** The region table exists once (`CITY_REGION`), consumed through the single `locality` accessor; the OpenAPI doc description restates the rule for the API contract, which is the appropriate place for it, not a code duplication.\n- **Nothing becomes a catch-all.** Both `Owner` and `OwnerMapper` already own exactly this kind of method, so the additions fit rather than bloat.\n\nStructure is clean and additive; no changes needed."
